sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant RT as Router
    participant CK as Chokepoint
    participant DB as India LLM log and disclosure store
    participant NP as Network egress path
    participant MP as Model provider
    participant RJ as Reconciliation job
    participant IN as Incident channel
    RT->>CK: Envelope with subjects and typed context
    CK->>CK: Manifest filter, classification and tokenisation
    CK->>DB: One commit - tokenised log line plus one record per surviving subject
    DB-->>CK: Committed
    Note over CK,DB: No commit, no send. A failed commit blocks the call.
    CK->>NP: Request to the provider, tagged with the call id
    NP->>NP: Connection-level egress record, written outside the application code
    NP->>MP: Tokenised payload
    MP-->>CK: Completion, or an error after receipt
    CK->>DB: Outcome completed - answered, abstained, draft created or provider error
    loop Every reconcile interval
        RJ->>NP: Reads connection-level egress records
        RJ->>DB: Reads committed records for the same call ids
        RJ->>IN: A transmitted call with missing records raises DET-AI-15
    end
